=2 Walkthrough
!Pso'Xja-map6.jpg|right|Floor 1
!Pso'Xja-map5.jpg|right|Floor 2
!Pso'Xja-map7.jpg|right|Floor B1
* In {z:Upper Jeuno}, speak to {n:Migliorozz} (H-9), Temple of the Goddess) who will give you either a {@k} {k:Phoenix pearl} or a {@k} {k:Phoenix armlet}.
** Which item you obtain depends on your progress in {M:Chains of Promathia Missions|Chains of Promathia Missions|Chains of Promathia Missions}.
*** If you have beaten {M:Darkness Named|Promathia Mission 3-5|Darkness Named}, you will receive the {@k} {k:Phoenix pearl}. If you have not yet cleared it, you will receive the {@k} {k:Phoenix armlet} instead.
**** The quest progresses the same regardless of the key item you obtain.
* Head to {z:Beaucedine Glacier} and enter {z:Pso'Xja} from the tower at (G-9).
** The {p:Survival Guide} (Fauregandi Region) will be the closest quick travel to the tower. The {p:Unity Warp} Lv.125 will place you at (I-9) on the ramp going down to the east, a level below the tower.
* Go up the stairs and into the small room at (I-8) where you will find a **???**.
* When you examine the **???**, {m:Gargoyle-Iota|Gargoyle Iota} and {m:Gargoyle-Kappa|Gargoyle Kappa} will spawn.
** The doors to this room will close as soon as the NM's spawn and will only open once they are defeated.
** Both NM's can switch between physical and magical immunity at will. They will glow Blue or Yellow when they switch immunity.
* Examine the **???** once the NM's are defeated to obtain a {@k} {k:Blue bracelet}.
* Head down the stairs to (H-9) where you will find a blue door that only opens if you have a {@k} {k:Blue bracelet}.
** Note: The mention of blue or green doors are identified by the color of the light atop their door-ways. Depending on the players screen configuration these soft colors can sometimes look similar.
* Drop down the hole and head to (H-7) where you will find another **???**.
* Checking the **???** will spawn {m:Gargoyle-Lambda|Gargoyle Lambda} and {m:Gargoyle-Mu|Gargoyle Mu}.
** The doors to this room will close as soon as the NM's spawn and will only open once they are defeated.
** They have the exact same immunity as the previous NM's.
* Examine the **???** after the NM's are defeated to obtain a {@k} {k:Green bracelet}.
* Return back to the entrance of this tower in the room with the stairwell (I-8) or by whatever means is fastest for you:
** You can continue south into the circular room on the basement floor and follow the right wall until you're at the stairs at (G-7). These will bring you back to (H-7) on the map where you started, and you can navigate back down the hall.
** You can also warp out, return to the {p:Survival Guide} and come back in through the entrance from {z:Beaucedine Glacier}'s tower at (G-9).
* Return upstairs (I-8), go down this hall (where the you acquired the {@k} {k:Blue bracelet} earlier) towards the end of the path where a green door is on the right. It will open for you with the {@k} {k:Green bracelet}.
* Head to (G-8) where you will find a **Crystal Receptor**.
** This device temporarily creates a set of platforms that lets you cross the path on the floor below which last 120 seconds.
* Examine the **Crystal Receptor** and quickly head back down the hall you came from to drop down the hole you passed by (H-9), labeled "Drop B" on the map. Run West then North through the room with the platforms, then up the stairs (G-7), until you find an elevator going down (H-8)/(?-?).
* Head down the elevator and examine the **Avatar Gate** on the West side of the circular room you're in for a cutscene.
** Monsters at the bottom of this elevator ride down ({m:Diremite Assaulter}) near the 'Avatar Gate' aggro to sound even at level 99, though they will be trivial for any player in item level gear to defeat.
** Optional exit / alternative to warping: Opposite/East from the gate in the circular room, you can travel down a hall and then north to a glowing platform which will teleport you back to {z:Beaucedine Glacier}'s tower at (G-9).
* Return to {n:Migliorozz} for your reward.

